Implement user story SKY-004-dashboard: Create styled dashboard HTML and configure build to copy static assets

## Story Description
Create src/public/index.html as a real styled single-page dashboard with header, search form, result area, and client-side JS. Configure package.json with 'start' script (node dist/server.js) and 'build' script that produces dist/server.js and copies src/public/ into dist/public/ so the / route works in both dev (tsx) and built (node) modes.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/public/index.html exists as a styled single-page dashboard with a full-width solid-color header bar (e.g. blue #1a73e8) containing bold white title 'Skyscanner Dashboard' and a smaller subtitle ('Search flights via the Skyscanner API' or equivalent)
- Dashboard contains a centered white card (max-width ~700px, rounded corners, light border, padding) with a 2-column grid search form: 'From (IATA)' and 'To (IATA)' text inputs on row 1, 'Date' (native date input) and 'Adults' (number input, default 1) on row 2, each with a label above the input
- Dashboard has a full-width solid-color button below the grid (same color as header) labeled 'Search Flights'; a status/message area below showing light-red/pink banner with red text for errors, muted-gray line for empty results, and result count on success
- Dashboard client-side JavaScript submits the form via GET /search (no full page reload), disables the button while request is in flight, and renders returned flights into a results table or appropriate status message in the same page
- package.json contains a 'start' script with value 'node dist/server.js' and a 'build' script (tsup or equivalent) that produces dist/server.js
- package.json 'build' script copies src/public/ into dist/public/ as part of the build — after npm run build, dist/public/index.html exists
- npm run build && npm run start successfully starts the server; GET /health returns 200; GET / serves the real dashboard file from dist/public/index.html (not 404 or stale/hardcoded fallback)
- npx tsc --noEmit exits 0 with no type errors





